TAM-OPEN

Inspect and open a file, directory, or URL.

tam-open detects the target type and launches an appropriate viewer. GUI tools
detach; terminal tools run in the foreground. It does not require XDG for its
built-in handlers.

A file:// URL is percent-decoded and must name this machine (no host, or
localhost). A tool that cannot start is reported with exit status 127.
Program lookup and launching come from libtam.
